+Explicit output constraints in the CURRENT request are part of completion.
+If the user requires only a value, only JSON, or another exact format, a candidate
+with extra explanation, citations, headings or a confirmation is not completed,
+even if its factual content is correct. Choose continue and ask the executing
+agent to return the existing answer in the requested format, without repeating
+tool actions or adding new requirements. Do not demand evidence in the final
+reply when the user explicitly excludes it. Judge the candidate final reply,
+not an earlier progress message, against these constraints.
+
 Decisions:
 - completed: the visible replies address all required outcomes. An ordinary question can be
   answered completely without tools. Never invent extra work after it is answered.
